    ==================================================================
    FEATURE-004 Asset Management: AM-003 Depreciation Board Views
    ==================================================================

    Read-only depreciation schedule visualization for the
    ``account.asset.depreciation.line`` model. Provides list, kanban,
    graph, pivot, and search views plus a top-level window action
    ("Depreciation Board") wired into the asset management menu.

    PERFORMANCE TARGET (per AAP)
    ============================
    Full-schedule render of 480 periods (40 years x 12 months) in
    under 2 seconds. Compensating controls:

      * ``limit="80"`` on the list view paginates the initial render.
      * The model's ``cumulative_depreciation`` and ``net_book_value``
        fields are stored ``@api.depends`` computations (defined in
        ``models/account_asset_depreciation_line.py``), so board
        rendering is a pure read with no recomputation on every fetch.
      * The model's ``asset_id`` foreign key is indexed; the
        ``company_id`` related field is ``store=True, index=True``,
        making multi-company ``ir.rule`` filters execute as indexed
        equality checks.
      * The window action sets ``search_default_filter_due_today=1``
        so the initial dataset is pre-filtered to lines that are due
        today or in the past, keeping the first page small.

    ACCESS PATHS
    ============
    * Top-level menu: Accounting > Assets > Depreciation Board
      (wired in ``views/menuitem.xml`` via the action defined below).
    * Drill-down from the asset form's "View Depreciation Board"
      button (the asset model method ``action_view_depreciation_lines``
      returns an ``ir.actions.act_window`` targeting this same model).
    * Embedded read-only list on the asset form is defined inline in
      ``views/account_asset_views.xml`` (not this file); the list view
      below is used only for the standalone board.

    AAP RULE COMPLIANCE
    ===================
    * R-01 (Module Independence): No references to any sibling new
      module (``account_budget_management``, ``account_deferred_revenue``,
      ``account_payment_followup``) or to FEATURE-001/002 CE modules.
    * R-02 (No Enterprise Deps): No references to Odoo Enterprise
      addons (``account_asset``, ``account_accountant``, etc.).
    * R-03 (_inherit / _name): Views target a net-new model
      (``account.asset.depreciation.line``); no view inheritance via
      ``inherit_id``.
    * R-05 (No Core View Modification): No ``inherit_id`` on any
      ``<record>``; no extension of any core or FEATURE-001/002 view.
    * R-07 (No sudo): Not applicable, XML only.
    * R-09 (Module Folder Names): File lives under exactly
      ``addons/account_asset_management/views/``.

    ODOO 19.0 CONVENTIONS
    =====================
    * ``<list>`` element (Odoo 17+ canonical name) is used instead of
      the legacy ``<tree>`` alias.
    * ``column_invisible="1"`` (list context) is used for
      ``currency_id`` (needed by the Monetary widget but not displayed).
    * ``optional="show"`` / ``optional="hide"`` toggle user-visible
      default state of optional columns.
    * ``invisible="..."`` / ``readonly="..."`` / ``required="..."``
      expressions replace the legacy ``attrs`` attribute.
    * ``groups="base.group_multi_company"`` guards multi-company
      fields and filters.
    * XML relational operators are escaped: ``&gt;``, ``&lt;``.
    * Indentation is 4 spaces.
-->
<odoo>

    <!-- ==================================================================
         LIST VIEW (EXPORT: view_account_asset_depreciation_line_list)

         This is the declared export of this file. It powers the list
         (tree) rendering on the Depreciation Board action and is the
         first view in the action's ``view_mode``.

         * ``default_order`` matches the model's ``_order`` so the
           ORM and view agree on ordering.
         * Row-level decorations mirror the badge color coding so
           users get visual state cues when scanning many periods.
         * ``create="false"`` / ``delete="false"`` enforce the AM-003
           requirement that the board is READ-ONLY from the user's
           perspective: schedule lines are generated automatically
           when an asset is confirmed.
         * ``limit="80"`` is the performance-critical pagination cap.
         ================================================================== -->
    <record id="view_account_asset_depreciation_line_list" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">account.asset.depreciation.line.list</field>
        <field name="model">account.asset.depreciation.line</field>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <list string="Depreciation Schedule"
                  default_order="asset_id, sequence, depreciation_date"
                  decoration-success="state == 'posted'"
                  decoration-muted="state == 'skipped'"
                  decoration-info="state == 'draft'"
                  create="false"
                  delete="false"
                  limit="80">
                <field name="asset_id"
                       optional="show"/>
                <field name="sequence" string="Period"/>
                <field name="depreciation_date"/>
                <field name="depreciation_amount"
                       sum="Total Depreciation"/>
                <field name="cumulative_depreciation"/>
                <field name="net_book_value"/>
                <field name="state" widget="badge"
                       decoration-success="state == 'posted'"
                       decoration-muted="state == 'skipped'"
                       decoration-info="state == 'draft'"/>
                <field name="move_id"
                       optional="show"/>
                <field name="company_id"
                       groups="base.group_multi_company"
                       optional="hide"/>
                <field name="currency_id" column_invisible="1"/>
            </list>
        </field>
    </record>

    <!-- ==================================================================
         KANBAN VIEW

         Groups schedule lines by ``state`` so users can see, at a
         glance, how many periods are still pending vs posted vs
         skipped. The ``label_selection`` widget on the ``state``
         field renders a color-coded label inside each card.

         * ``default_group_by="state"`` places draft / posted /
           skipped into separate columns.
         * ``create="false"`` / ``delete="false"`` preserve the
           read-only posture from the list view.
         * ``o_kanban_small_column`` keeps columns compact so many
           periods fit in the viewport.
         ================================================================== -->
    <record id="view_account_asset_depreciation_line_kanban" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">account.asset.depreciation.line.kanban</field>
        <field name="model">account.asset.depreciation.line</field>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <kanban default_group_by="state"
                    create="false"
                    delete="false"
                    class="o_kanban_small_column">
                <field name="asset_id"/>
                <field name="sequence"/>
                <field name="depreciation_date"/>
                <field name="depreciation_amount"/>
                <field name="cumulative_depreciation"/>
                <field name="net_book_value"/>
                <field name="state"/>
                <field name="currency_id"/>
                <field name="move_id"/>
                <templates>
                    <t t-name="kanban-box">
                        <div t-attf-class="oe_kanban_card oe_kanban_global_click o_kanban_card_compact">
                            <div class="o_kanban_record_top">
                                <div class="o_kanban_record_headings">
                                    <strong><field name="asset_id"/></strong>
                                    <span class="text-muted">Period <field name="sequence"/></span>
                                </div>
                                <field name="state" widget="label_selection"
                                       options="{'classes': {'posted': 'success', 'skipped': 'default', 'draft': 'info'}}"/>
                            </div>
                            <div class="o_kanban_record_body">
                                <field name="depreciation_date" widget="date"/>
                                <div class="row">
                                    <div class="col-6">
                                        <strong>Amount:</strong>
                                        <field name="depreciation_amount" widget="monetary"/>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="col-6">
                                        <strong>NBV:</strong>
                                        <field name="net_book_value" widget="monetary"/>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </t>
                </templates>
            </kanban>
        </field>
    </record>

    <!-- ==================================================================
         GRAPH VIEW

         Time-series chart of monthly depreciation expense and the
         rising cumulative-depreciation curve. Two measures overlayed
         on a line chart gives users a quick visual read on both
         periodic expense pattern and the running total.

         * ``type="line"`` is appropriate for time-based progression.
         * ``sample="1"`` shows illustrative placeholder data when
           the dataset is empty, preserving chart affordance.
         * ``interval="month"`` on ``depreciation_date`` aggregates
           monthly, the natural cadence for most depreciation
           schedules.
         ================================================================== -->
    <record id="view_account_asset_depreciation_line_graph" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">account.asset.depreciation.line.graph</field>
        <field name="model">account.asset.depreciation.line</field>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <graph string="Depreciation Trend" type="line" sample="1">
                <field name="depreciation_date" interval="month" type="row"/>
                <field name="depreciation_amount" type="measure"/>
                <field name="cumulative_depreciation" type="measure"/>
            </graph>
        </field>
    </record>

    <!-- ==================================================================
         PIVOT VIEW

         Rows = asset, columns = year, value = depreciation amount.
         Gives finance users a natural matrix for cross-asset annual
         depreciation comparison, with native drill-up / drill-down
         on the year axis.

         * ``interval="year"`` on the column axis is the most
           commonly requested aggregation for multi-asset reporting.
         * Users can switch to month / quarter at runtime via the
           pivot view controls if a finer cadence is needed.
         ================================================================== -->
    <record id="view_account_asset_depreciation_line_pivot" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">account.asset.depreciation.line.pivot</field>
        <field name="model">account.asset.depreciation.line</field>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <pivot string="Depreciation Schedule" sample="1">
                <field name="asset_id" type="row"/>
                <field name="depreciation_date" interval="year" type="col"/>
                <field name="depreciation_amount" type="measure"/>
            </pivot>
        </field>
    </record>

    <!-- ==================================================================
         SEARCH VIEW

         Implements the AM-003 acceptance criteria for filtering,
         sorting, and grouping the depreciation schedule:

           * AC4: State filters (pending / posted / skipped)
           * AC5: Date-range filters (due today or past, this year,
                  next year) using ``context_today()`` and
                  ``relativedelta`` expressions evaluated by the
                  Odoo ORM search domain compiler.

         Date-filter domains use escaped ``&gt;=`` and ``&lt;=``
         because XML does not permit raw ``>`` and ``<`` inside
         attribute values.

         Group-by options align to the three most useful aggregation
         dimensions: by asset (one asset, many periods), by state
         (pending / posted / skipped buckets), and by time (month,
         year). The multi-company group-by is guarded so it only
         appears for users in multi-company databases.
         ================================================================== -->
    <record id="view_account_asset_depreciation_line_search" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">account.asset.depreciation.line.search</field>
        <field name="model">account.asset.depreciation.line</field>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <search string="Depreciation Schedule">
                <!-- Primary search fields (AM-003 AC5 / AC6) -->
                <field name="asset_id"/>
                <field name="move_id"/>
                <field name="depreciation_date"/>

                <!-- State filters (AM-003 AC4) -->
                <separator/>
                <filter name="filter_draft"
                        string="Pending"
                        domain="[('state', '=', 'draft')]"/>
                <filter name="filter_posted"
                        string="Posted"
                        domain="[('state', '=', 'posted')]"/>
                <filter name="filter_skipped"
                        string="Skipped"
                        domain="[('state', '=', 'skipped')]"/>

                <!-- Date filters (AM-003 AC5) -->
                <separator/>
                <filter name="filter_due_today"
                        string="Due Today or Past"
                        domain="[('depreciation_date', '&lt;=', context_today().strftime('%Y-%m-%d'))]"/>
                <filter name="filter_this_year"
                        string="This Year"
                        domain="[
                            ('depreciation_date', '&gt;=', (context_today() + relativedelta(month=1, day=1)).strftime('%Y-%m-%d')),
                            ('depreciation_date', '&lt;=', (context_today() + relativedelta(month=12, day=31)).strftime('%Y-%m-%d'))
                        ]"/>
                <filter name="filter_next_year"
                        string="Next Year"
                        domain="[
                            ('depreciation_date', '&gt;=', (context_today() + relativedelta(years=1, month=1, day=1)).strftime('%Y-%m-%d')),
                            ('depreciation_date', '&lt;=', (context_today() + relativedelta(years=1, month=12, day=31)).strftime('%Y-%m-%d'))
                        ]"/>

                <!-- Group-by options -->
                <separator/>
                <group expand="0" string="Group By">
                    <filter name="groupby_asset"
                            string="Asset"
                            context="{'group_by': 'asset_id'}"/>
                    <filter name="groupby_state"
                            string="Status"
                            context="{'group_by': 'state'}"/>
                    <filter name="groupby_month"
                            string="Month"
                            context="{'group_by': 'depreciation_date:month'}"/>
                    <filter name="groupby_year"
                            string="Year"
                            context="{'group_by': 'depreciation_date:year'}"/>
                    <filter name="groupby_company"
                            string="Company"
                            context="{'group_by': 'company_id'}"
                            groups="base.group_multi_company"/>
                </group>
            </search>
        </field>
    </record>

    <!-- ==================================================================
         WINDOW ACTION (top-level "Depreciation Board" menu entry)

         Presents the four rendering modes (list, kanban, graph,
         pivot) with the search view above, and auto-activates the
         "Due Today or Past" filter on open so the first page is
         scoped to actionable lines. This is the performance-critical
         default: without it, opening the board on a company with
         many assets could render tens of thousands of future periods
         before the user has had a chance to filter.

         The help text guides users who open the board on an empty
         database to the asset creation workflow, since schedule
         lines are generated from confirmed assets rather than
         directly created here.
         ================================================================== -->
    <record id="action_account_asset_depreciation_line" model="ir.actions.act_window">
        <field name="name">Depreciation Board</field>
        <field name="res_model">account.asset.depreciation.line</field>
        <field name="view_mode">list,kanban,graph,pivot</field>
        <field name="search_view_id" ref="view_account_asset_depreciation_line_search"/>
        <field name="context">{'search_default_filter_due_today': 1}</field>
        <field name="help" type="html">
            <p class="o_view_nocontent_smiling_face">
                No depreciation lines yet.
            </p>
            <p>
                Depreciation schedule lines are generated automatically when an asset is confirmed.
                Create and confirm an asset first, and the system will pre-compute the complete
                depreciation schedule based on the asset's method, useful life, and salvage value.
            </p>
        </field>
    </record>

</odoo>
